\caption(Every mean variance is below 0.01. The computed unit-KL table and decomposition retain the different scales and distinguish analytic KL from sampled density ratios.)
\alttext(Four low variance points for each schedule lie below a horizontal 0.01 activity threshold; both runs have zero active mean coordinates.)

The mixture calculation uses all 288 fitting posteriors and their four aligned draws, not a
minibatch reweighting or a held-out population estimate. Constant fit analytic KL is 0.030596506;
sampled conditional 0.031579444 decomposes into information 0.006069839 plus aggregate 0.025509605.
Warmup gives 0.031146600 analytic,0.031241785 sampled,0.007030088 information and 0.024211697 aggregate.
Neither schedule supplies evidence of a useful language code in this short run.

> Fixed true-prefix code ablations and free decoding

Hold all true previous-token prefixes fixed and decode with one posterior draw, zero code,
a one-row cyclic shuffle of posterior codes, or the matching standard-normal prior draw.
This isolates code changes without changing the available prefixes. NLL here logs Float32
probabilities in Float64, preserving the original diagnostic; it is distinct from the
four-draw log-softmax scoring path above. Underflow is not repaired or clipped.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/collapse_ablations.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto chart  = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  std::print(
      "| schedule | code | fixed-prefix teacher NLL | max probability change from posterior "
      "|\n|---|---|---:|---:|\n");
  for (const std::string name : {"constant", "warmup"}) {
    const auto a    = n::load_npz("build/posterior_collapse/" + name + "/ablations.npz");
    auto       find = [&](const std::string& key) {
      for (const auto& [k, v] : a)
        if (k == key)
          return v;
      throw std::runtime_error(key);
    };
    auto                tokens    = find("tokens").to_vector<int>();
    auto                reference = find("posterior_probability").to_vector<float>();
    std::vector<double> values;
    for (const std::string code : {"posterior", "zero", "shuffled", "prior"}) {
      auto   p   = find(code + "_probability").to_vector<float>();
      double sum = 0, effect = 0;
      for (std::size_t i = 0; i < tokens.size(); ++i)
        if (tokens[i])
          sum -= std::log(double(p[i * 19 + tokens[i]]));
      for (std::size_t i = 0; i < p.size(); ++i)
        effect = std::max(effect, std::abs(double(p[i]) - reference[i]));
      values.push_back(sum / 72);
      std::print("| {} | {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n", name, code, sum / 72, effect);
    }
    const auto color = name == "constant" ? dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235} : dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38};
    chart.lines({1, 2, 3, 4}, values, name, color, 2).points({1, 2, 3, 4}, values, "", color, 5);
  }
  chart.x_ticks({1, 2, 3, 4}, {"posterior", "zero", "shuffled", "prior"})
      .title("Fixed true prefixes / one matched code draw / zoomed NLL")
      .x_label("code supplied to the same decoder")
      .y_label("teacher NLL / nats per sentence")
      .y_limits(18.65, 18.8)
      .save_svg("build/collapse_ablations.svg");
}
```
