The mean-code outputs repeatedly produce “a a [eos]”; free posterior outputs also omit grammar
roles or repeat tokens. True-prefix teacher reconstruction and free generation answer
different questions. No warmup-superiority, fluency or semantic-usefulness claim follows from
these three-epoch, single-seed fits. This report illustrates measurements and controls for
weak latent use, rather than assuming a chosen schedule cures it.

> Reproduce and independently verify

Run all C++ blocks in order with the checkout's matching installed library. Native preparation
uses the shared configurable cache; no external checkout or Python preparation is needed.
All 35 source archives/2,265,740 array values, complete TSVs and non-timing JSON values are
checked against the untouched run. The optional NumPy development oracle independently
checks all first BPTT derivatives/first Adam, all eighteen saved endpoints, every eligible
common validation score, explicit noise and signed mixture/generation/ablation controls:

```
python3 scripts/check_sequence_variational_autoencoder.py docs/mepml/examples/nn/2_autoencoders/2.2_variational_autoencoders/build/posterior_collapse --json build/nn-report-conversion/posterior_report/oracle.json
```

